<title>INDIA: Indian soybean down on sluggish demand, trade slow.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean down on sluggish demand, trade slow.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices weakened further in central Indian markets on limited demand from processing plants, while arrivals were limited due to rain, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>They said prices were down by 150-200 rupees per tonne in lacklustre trade.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices rose 100 rupees per tonne on good demand in local markets. Trading activity was limited and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were steady in thin trading.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $265-266 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was slightly down on limited export demand and quoted at $95-97 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for exports and was 3,175-3,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. The undertone was steady.</p>
